# BookmarkFeeder — LOCAL docker compose run
#
# Runs the production artifact on your own machine: same images, same compose, same wiring as the
# NAS. Use it to prove a release actually starts before shipping it.
#
#   cp docker/.env.local.template docker/.env
#   docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yaml up -d
#   open http://localhost:8081
#
# For day-to-day development use the AppHost instead (`dotnet run --project BookmarkFeeder.AppHost`)
# — it gives hot reload and the dev dashboard. This is for testing what actually ships.
#
# These are throwaway local values, not secrets. Never reuse them on the NAS.

# Auth0 tenant. NOT secrets - a tenant domain, an API audience and a public SPA client id are all
# published in any browser bundle. But they ARE per-tenant, so point them at your own; see
# docs/deployment.md for the two CLI commands that create them.
#
# The browser extension needs none of this: it authenticates with a key you mint in the web app.
AUTH0_DOMAIN=usualexpat.uk.auth0.com
AUTH0_AUDIENCE=https://api.bookmarkfeeder
AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=LO0F1SDrYKFqS3GIrScJSyFR3q0D9YCM

# Only if you are UPGRADING an install from before accounts existed (before 0.2.0): the Auth0 subject
# (e.g. google-oauth2|1234...) or email of the person who should get the bookmarks that were
# already there. Signup is open, so the collection is never simply handed to whoever signs in
# first. Your subject is shown in the web app under Settings. Leave empty on a fresh install.
AUTH0_LEGACY_OWNER=

# Local Postgres password. Only ever reachable from inside the compose network.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=local-dev-password

# Published port for the gateway — the ONLY way in. http://localhost:8081
# Both sides of the mapping and the gateway's own HTTP_PORTS come from this one value.
# 8081 to match the NAS, where 8080 is taken by Glance.
GATEWAY_PORT=8081

# The API's port INSIDE its own container. Never published, so it cannot collide with anything on
# the host — 8080 here is unrelated to the gateway's published port and needs no change.
WEBAPI_PORT=8080

# Where Postgres writes its cluster. Defaults to ./data/postgres next to the compose file
# (docker/data/postgres — gitignored). Delete that directory to start from an empty database.
#POSTGRES_DATA_PATH=./data/postgres

# Images. Either the tags a release pushed, or whatever ./scripts/docker-build.sh built locally —
# docker prefers a local image with the same name, so a local build needs no change here.
WEBAPI_IMAGE=docker.io/mgpeter/bookmarkfeeder-webapi:0.3.33
GATEWAY_IMAGE=docker.io/mgpeter/bookmarkfeeder-gateway:0.3.33
WEB_IMAGE=docker.io/mgpeter/bookmarkfeeder-web:0.3.33
